# 7. Current architecture

Right now you've effectively got:

```text
                SHARE TRADING

Provider
Commonwealth Bank
commonwealth-bank-of-australia
          │
          ▼
Offering
CommSec
commsec
          │
          ├── Profile
          │   /share-trading/commsec
          │
          └── Comparison
              commsec-vs-stake


                  CRYPTO

Provider
CoinSpot
coinspot
          │
          ▼
Offering
CoinSpot Crypto Exchange
coinspot-exchange
          │
          │
          └── ignored for public identity
                   ↓
Provider.slug used instead
                   ↓
          /crypto/exchanges/coinspot
```

That's why it feels odd.

The schema says Offering is the product, but crypto routing still behaves like the older Provider-centric architecture.

